ough  to just spill it all out the  misconceptions that people have about  plus-sized women we are lazy we have low  self-esteem we don't care about our  parents we are non-existent and we exist  this is Who I am plus size and fabulous  [Music]  lion dancing dates back to the Tang  Dynasty in China I was really meant to  wore off the evil spirits and welcome  the good ones I am a 20-something year  old millennial but I still hold this  piece of tradition grab three rings and  make three lines I was born and raised  in Chinatown we do have a lot of the  Chinese traditions that they've come  over and carried on and passed on to us  line dancing is really important to  chine home because it is a traditional  sport it's something that a lot of  people do come out and they celebrate  around Chinese New Year typically  includes at least two people percent in  a line you'll have somebody who plays  the lion head and then somebody will  play the tail when you first come in you  walk through the door you can't just  pick up a lion head it takes about a  year for you to be able to work your way  up to that level Kung Fu is the  foundation of lion dance their stances  and their leg work it's extremely  important we're having you trained in  your footwork in your stances making  sure that you're strong enough to  physically hold yourself through a  routine but also a lion head because a  lion head is heavy specifically anywhere  between fifteen to thirty pounds  [Music]  typically we teach different routines  for each of the lines just because you  never know which one you're going to  play it  you can see this line dancing in the  streets anytime where there is a  community event will usually partaking  them in Chinatown a lot of people are  familiar with line dancing and they get  really pumped and excited for it so just  the energy in the atmosphere for me is  ten times better  it's really important for all of us of  that we are educated about line dancing  we do carry it on