agrado s profundo  Constanta meant a not a repeat a they  like sustained sia de los cielos entre  nosotros  [Music]  dance is something that comes in every  last one of us from birth what we do is  take that and give them an opportunity  to personalize it and then it empowers  us to dance at this level my name is  Melvin Mitchell Aiko and I'm the founder  of Northwest tap connection our mission  is to close the gap for underserved  communities with an emphasis on children  of color and really just open that door  for young people who would not be able  to have accessibility to the arts  because of cost to have those  opportunities that are it enriching when  I started off with staff I was working  for the set of Police Department and my  goal was their children that I got to  see on a weekly basis I would never see  across my desk tap dancing is the  foundation of our organization I strive  to make sure that children understand  that it is a dance form that comes out  of black culture  it comes out of protests and we have to  appreciate it embrace it and protect it  as we pass it down northwest tab is a  race and social justice oriented studio  and being an african-american male I  don't think had I danced at another  studio that I would have been surrounded  by so many fellow african-americans and  I feel like that has given me the  confidence to feel comfortable in my  skin and normal everyday life I don't  really like talking very much but when  it comes to dancing I am able to just  communicate in a way that touches people  rather than what they're just hearing my  feelings as I watched young people dance  there is this sense of pride for the  work that they do but then at the same  time there's this sense of fear and  trouble for me how much longer will we  continue with this struggle dance is  such an empowering tool we are  communities of many colors many genders  identifications but we are one drew  these children that dance we're creating  a new tomorrow  [